<PageLayout title="Local Library Folder Structure & Format — TotalRecalls" description="Learn how TotalRecalls organizes your local library folder: Markdown and JSON file hierarchy, provider subdirectories, and metadata manifests." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Guides", href: "/guides/" }, { label: "Library" }]}>
  <h1>TotalRecalls Library Format</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    TotalRecalls stores every conversation in a clean, predictable, and vendor-neutral directory hierarchy on your local
    drive. By default, files are placed in <code>%USERPROFILE%\TotalRecalls-download\Library\</code>, but you can select
    any internal drive, external SSD, or network-attached storage volume.
  </p>

  <h2>Directory Structure Overview</h2>
  <p>
    The library organizes chats into dedicated subfolders by provider, with a central metadata tracking directory:
  </p>
  <pre><code>%USERPROFILE%\TotalRecalls-download\Library\
├── chatgpt\
│   ├── 2026-08-09-how-to-refactor-react.md
│   └── 2026-08-09-how-to-refactor-react.json
├── claude\
│   ├── 2026-08-10-distributed-consensus.md
│   └── 2026-08-10-distributed-consensus.json
├── perplexity\
├── gemini\
├── grok\
├── deepseek\
├── mistral\
├── qwen\
├── metadata\
│   └── export-manifest.json
└── README.txt</code></pre>

  <h2>The Dual-File Architecture (.md + .json)</h2>
  <p>
    Every single conversation is saved as an atomic pair of files sharing an identical base filename formatted
    as <code>YYYY-MM-DD-sanitized-title</code>:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Human-Readable Markdown (<code>.md</code>):</strong> Structured plain text formatted with standard
      CommonMark syntax. Each file begins with a YAML frontmatter block recording the original conversation title,
      source provider, model name, creation timestamp, and unique conversation identifier. Message turns are rendered
      with clear role headers (<code>### User</code>, <code>### Assistant</code>), code blocks preserve their original syntax
      highlighting tags, and mathematical LaTeX expressions stay intact.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Lossless Raw JSON (<code>.json</code>):</strong> A complete, uncompressed JSON object containing the exact
      original message tree, full token metadata, tool calls, thinking/reasoning blocks (such as DeepSeek-R1 traces),
      and web search citation URLs. This structure guarantees that future tools, custom parsers, and vector indexers
      have access to the raw payload without information loss.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Metadata Manifest (<code>metadata/export-manifest.json</code>)</h2>
  <p>
    TotalRecalls maintains an incremental manifest file to enable fast synchronization and deduplication:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "last_export": "2026-11-12T14:30:00Z",
  "providers": {
    "chatgpt": { "conversation_count": 106, "file_pairs": 106 },
    "claude": { "conversation_count": 84, "file_pairs": 84 }
  }
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Third-Party Integration &amp; Longevity</h2>
  <p>
    Because TotalRecalls writes standard text files rather than a proprietary database blob:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Obsidian:</strong> Open the <code>Library\</code> folder directly as an Obsidian Vault to explore your chats with bi-directional wikilinks and graph views.</li>
    <li><strong>Notion:</strong> Use Notion's native Markdown import utility to bring research threads into shared workspaces.</li>
    <li><strong>Windows Search &amp; ripgrep:</strong> Instant full-text search across thousands of files directly from Windows File Explorer or developer command-line tools.</li>
    <li><strong>Local Backups:</strong> Compatible with Windows File History, OneDrive, Backblaze, and Git version control out of the box.</li>
  </ul>
</PageLayout>
